<title>JAPAN: TENNIS-FRANCE BEAT JAPAN 4-1 IN FED CUP TIE.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-FRANCE BEAT JAPAN 4-1 IN FED CUP TIE.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>France beat Japan 4-1 in their Fed Cup tennis World Group 1 tie after winning the doubles and sharing the reverse singles on Sunday.</p>
<p>Results (French names first):</p>
<p>Played Sunday</p>
<p>Alexandra Fusai/Anne Sidot beat Naoko Kijimuta/Kyoko Nagatsuka</p>
<p>7-5 6-4</p>
<p>Nathalie Tauziat beat Naoko Sawamatsu 7-5 4-6 17-15</p>
<p>Mary Pierce lost to Ai Sugiyama 5-7 7-6 (9-7) 4-6</p>
<p>Played Saturday</p>
<p>Pierce beat Sawamatsu 6-0 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>Tauziat beat Ai Sugiyama 4-6 7-5 6-4</p>
</text>
